==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|buoys up|buoying up|buoyed up}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive|figurative}} To [[uplift]], [[hearten]], [[inspire]] or [[raise]] the [[spirits]] of.
#* '''1796''', {{w|Edmund Burke}}, ''A letter from the Right Honourable Edmund Burke to a noble lord: on the attacks made upon him and his pension'', London: J. Owen and F. & C. Rivington, p. ,<sup>[http://name.umdl.umich.edu/004798579.0001.000]</sup>
#*: I have supported with very great zeal, and I am told with some degree of success, those opinions, or if his Grace likes another expression better, those old prejudices, which '''buoy up''' the ponderous mass of his nobility, wealth, and title.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|transitive}} To keep [[afloat]]; to provide with [[buoyancy]].

